170	\begin{definition}[Restricted diagonal lines test]\label{def:restricted-diagonal-lines-test}
171		\lean{MIPStarRE.LDT.RestrictedDiagonalSample, MIPStarRE.LDT.MainInductionStep.RestrictedSymStrat.diagonalFailureProbability}
172		\leanok
173		Consider the $(m,q,d)$ low individual degree test. For $j \in \{1,\dots,m\}$, the $j$-restricted diagonal lines test is the diagonal lines test conditioned on $i=j$. In particular, the $m$-restricted diagonal lines test is the diagonal lines test in which the sampled line is a uniformly random line in $\F_q^m$.
