689		\uses{def:dot-product-orthogonal, def:subfield-trace}
690		Let $V$ be a subspace of $\F_q^k$ and let $\omega = e^{2\pi i/p}$, where
691		$p$ is the characteristic of $\F_q$ and $\tr = \tr_{q \to p}$. For all
692		$v \notin V^\perp$,
693		\[
694			\E_{\bu \sim V}\, \omega^{\tr(\bu \cdot v)} = 0\;,
695		\]
696		where the expectation is over a uniformly random vector $\bu$ in $V$.
697	\end{lemma}
698	\begin{proof}
699		This is Fact 3.2 of \cite{Natarajan2018NEEXP}. Since $v \notin V^\perp$,
700		the $\F_q$-linear functional $u \mapsto u \cdot v$ is not identically zero
701		on $V$, hence surjective onto $\F_q$; composing with the nonzero map $\tr$
702		shows that there is $u_0 \in V$ with $\tr(u_0 \cdot v) \neq 0$. Writing $C$
703		for the expectation, translation invariance of the uniform distribution on
704		$V$ gives
705		$C = \E_{\bu \sim V}\, \omega^{\tr((\bu + u_0) \cdot v)}
706		= \omega^{\tr(u_0 \cdot v)}\, C$, and $\omega^{\tr(u_0 \cdot v)} \neq 1$
707		forces $C = 0$.
708	\end{proof}
